<section id="principles">
  <p class="eyebrow"><span class="num">05</span> Principles <span class="line"></span></p>
  <h2 class="lede"><span class="marker"></span>Four things I believe after two decades of shipping. They aren&rsquo;t slogans &mdash; they&rsquo;re <em>how AR Data picks engagements.</em></h2>

  <div class="principles">
    <div class="principle">
      <div class="num">/ 01</div>
      <blockquote>Production is the <em>only</em> thing that counts.</blockquote>
      <div class="gloss">A demo is a hypothesis. A deployed system that survives a Monday morning is a result. We measure ourselves against the second.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="principle">
      <div class="num">/ 02</div>
      <blockquote>If you can&rsquo;t <em>roll back</em>, you can&rsquo;t ship.</blockquote>
      <div class="gloss">Every system we deploy has a reverse gear. Migrations are reversible, agents have kill-switches, decisions are traceable. Forward velocity without rollback is a bug, not a feature.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="principle">
      <div class="num">/ 03</div>
      <blockquote>AI tooling moves fast. <em>Maintenance</em> doesn&rsquo;t.</blockquote>
      <div class="gloss">Generated code is cheap; the system it ships into still has to be operable on a Tuesday in three years. We pair AI speed with the engineering judgment that makes it durable.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="principle">
      <div class="num">/ 04</div>
      <blockquote>No bench. No <em>prototype-and-disappear.</em></blockquote>
      <div class="gloss">Bootstrapped means we only take work we can actually deliver. The team that wins your engagement is the team that builds it &mdash; and stands behind it after.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="principle wide">
      <div class="num">/ 05 &middot; FOUNDATIONAL</div>
      <blockquote>Agentic workflow. <em>Human drives the outcome.</em> AI supports.</blockquote>
      <div class="gloss">An agent is a tool, not a decision-maker. The human owns the goal, the success criteria, the trade-offs, and the sign-off. Agents accelerate the work between those decisions &mdash; they do not replace them. Every system we ship makes that boundary explicit: who decides, who executes, who reviews. Get this wrong and you don&rsquo;t have an agentic workflow; you have an unattended liability.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

